This group project is the final assessment for COS30045 Data Visualisation (worth 40% of the total course mark). We analysed and built an interactive web-based data visualisation using Australian road crash hospitalisation data (2011–2021) published by BITRE.
The core focus is to explore disparities in road crash related hospital injuries between First Nations peoples and non-Indigenous Australians, including trends over time, risk groups (age, road user type, residential remoteness), and geographic differences across Australian states.
